 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6100+) It also records compact production and military interval flows plus exact civic, effective state-religion, and war-plan transitions. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6101+) Technology-acquisition rows also identify whether each technology came from research, trade, a free choice, a goody hut, a Great Person, espionage, a random event, technology sharing, a team merge, inheritance, Advanced Start, Barbarian research, game setup, debug tools, or an unknown Python/script source. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6102+) Each log also identifies whether the session is a new or loaded single-player, scenario, network, Hotseat, PBEM, Pitboss, or replay game, including its multiplayer turn options. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6103+) It also synthesizes one summary for every war between civilization teams, including declaration and peace context, elapsed turns, war-success changes, units destroyed and their total production cost, city-plot battle wins, and cities/population captured. Wars already active when a save is loaded are explicitly partial, while wars still active at victory or autoplay end remain marked ongoing rather than being misreported as peace. A full turn-474 test matched all 115 declarations to exactly 91 ordinary-peace summaries, 4 capitulations, 13 state-change/elimination summaries, and 7 wars still ongoing at victory.
