+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6119+) **Autoplay can continue through harmless notices and explain exactly how it ended:** an active player's defeat could transfer human control during an ongoing autoplay and make the EXE pause behind an OK-only "it's your turn" prompt; ordinary informational text notices could also require an unnecessary click. An XML-tunable option now omits only these no-decision prompts during autoplay, without accepting or suppressing diplomacy, events, civics, war, launch, production, technology, or other gameplay choices. `SASGameRecord` also records each autoplay request's requested/completed turns, starting turn/player, explicit end cause, and active-player-change counts, while separate `ACTIVE_PLAYER_CHANGED` rows show exactly when and from/to whom each transfer occurred. In the full confirming run, player 0 changed to player 1 on turn 392 with 109 autoplay turns remaining; the handoff prompt was suppressed, and the final row reported one player change plus `endCause=VICTORY` and 500 completed turns from the 501-turn request because a Time victory ended the run first. A separate three-request test also correctly distinguished two scheduled completions from a manual interruption: the interrupted 31-turn request stopped after 18 completed turns with 13 remaining and reported `endCause=USER_INTERRUPTED`. See [KI#203](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#203---improved-ai-auto-play-could-pause-behind-harmless-informational-popups-and-its-logs-could-not-reliably-explain-why-a-run-ended).
