 featureless land keep feature and bonus pictures readable without overlaying geography. Each layer also reports its logical-cell total, exact drawing-character total, and per-symbol cell counts, so broad composition and change can be measured without manually counting the picture; horizontal visual repetition does not inflate these cell counts. Separate structured rows directly record player pollution, its sources, city health, global warming, and exact bonuses; the maps supply spatial context. Clean fixed-width rows preserve the generated map's proportions in horizontal, square, or vertical maps; legends map configurable symbols and runtime numeric IDs to terrain/feature/bonus types, while political symbols map to player IDs whose setup rows provide the civilization and displayed player name. XML defines control the picture bounds, monospace-width correction, and validated symbols. Each picture is enabled by default because the spatial context is useful to humans and LLMs, but can be disabled independently to reduce log size and clutter.
